      "id": "SKP-001",
      "concern": "Auto-mode sample starvation (mathematical impossibility of exiting cold-start)",
      "severity": "CRITICAL",
      "severity_score": 950,
      "why_matters": "The condition `min(b[\"n\"] for b in buckets_24h.values()) < SAMPLE_GATE_N` requires ALL buckets to have >= 20 samples to enter band comparison. However, cold-start statically routes to a single default (`headless` or `recommended_for`). Because the non-default bucket receives zero traffic, it will never reach 20 samples, permanently locking the system in cold-start and defeating the entire auto-mode mechanism.",
      "location": "§5.2 `_resolve_auto`",
      "recommendation": "Change the sample gate logic to evaluate the default bucket's success rate first, and implement an epsilon-greedy exploration strategy (e.g., route 5% of traffic to the starved bucket) to organically build the required sample size for comparison.",
      "source": "tertiary_skeptic"
    },
    {
      "id": "SKP-005",
