      "severity_score": 790,
      "why_matters": "A migration race can reset an OPEN circuit to CLOSED or preserve stale failure state over current state, causing either outage amplification or unnecessary provider blackouts. The SDD lists this as a carry-in rather than defining safe semantics.",
      "location": "§3.3 Circuit-breaker state file schema; §5.3 `_migrate_legacy_state_if_present`; §10.5 SKP-001 v1.2",
      "recommendation": "Define idempotent migration rules normatively: if the new http_api bucket exists, it wins; legacy files are ignored or archived, never copied over active state. Explicitly exclude symlinks from legacy-file migration scans and add race tests for preexisting new state.",
      "source": "tertiary_skeptic"
    },
