      "why_matters": "The live stress test uses `rsync` to move `$ORIG_HOME/.config/<cli>` and relies on a `trap` to restore it. If the test runner suffers a hard crash (SIGKILL, OOM, power loss), the trap will not execute, permanently deleting the operator's real CLI authentication state and tokens.",
      "location": "§7.6 Stress-test isolation",
      "recommendation": "Do not move or modify the original directory. Instead, copy the original config to the ephemeral `$HOME`, run the test against the ephemeral `$HOME`, and simply delete the ephemeral directory afterward.",
      "source": "tertiary_skeptic"
